 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Back in the kitchen at Claude Monet, Senya and Fedya, two of Barinov's cooks, are comparing their new, polite chef, Elena, with the old one. Then Barinov comes back in a terrible temper. It's in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ну, как тебе новый шеф-повар?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Она кажется мне немного скучной.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Зато она спокойная и вежливая.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Это правда, она никогда не кричит.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "С ней на кухне тихо и приятно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Бездельники! Огрызки! Что вы делаете?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я вернулся навести полный порядок!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Шеф, мы просто чистили рыбу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы очень рады видеть вас!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Прекратите болтать и берите ножи!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Кто разрешил вам стоять без дела?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Мы сейчас всё нарежем, шеф.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Быстро за работу, живо!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Slowly now. The first half is a quiet chat, and the second half is Barinov.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Ну, как тебе новый шеф-повар?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, how do you like the new head chef?' The question ends with the title ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "шеф-повар",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", which is an imported word for head chef.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Она кажется мне немного скучной.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'She seems a bit boring to me.' He finds the new situation quite ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "скучной",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", a word for dull or boring.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Зато она спокойная и вежливая.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'On the other hand she is calm and polite.' He prefers how their new boss is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "вежливая",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the word for polite or courteous.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Это правда, она никогда не кричит.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'That is true, she never yells.' It is a relief that nobody ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "кричит",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning yells or shouts loudly.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "С ней на кухне тихо и приятно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'With her the kitchen is quiet and pleasant.' Now the working environment feels remarkably ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "тихо",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning quiet and peaceful.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Бездельники! Огрызки! Что вы делаете?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Slackers! Scraps! What are you doing?' The angry entrance starts by shouting ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Бездельники",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", a harsh insult for people who do no work.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Я вернулся навести полный порядок!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I returned to restore complete order!' He announces his arrival by stating he ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "вернулся",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning returned or came back.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Шеф, мы просто чистили рыбу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef, we were just cleaning the fish.' Trying to look busy, they claim they ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "чистили",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning they were cleaning or scaling.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы очень рады видеть вас!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We are very glad to see you!' They try to smooth things over by saying they are ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "рады",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning glad or happy.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Прекратите болтать и берите ножи!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Stop chatting and take your knives!' He orders them to pick up their ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "ножи",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the tools they need for cutting food.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Кто разрешил вам стоять без дела?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Who permitted you to stand idle?' The boss demands to know who ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "разрешил",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning allowed or gave permission.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Мы сейчас всё нарежем, шеф.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We will chop everything right now, chef.' Promising immediate action, they say they will ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "нарежем",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning chop or slice up a batch of ingredients.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Быстро за работу, живо!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Get to work quickly, lively!' Barking a final order, he adds ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "живо",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning lively or look sharp. Now the whole thing again, calm and then loud.",
   "gap": 0.9
